{"id":"city-purchase-deeds","title":"The recorded deeds behind the buildings the City bought","question":"For each purchase the Board approved, when did the City take title, who signed the property over, and how often had it changed hands just before?","finding":"The recorder's index was printed for 40 of the purchases; 32 show the deed to the City on the printed lot. The median time from the Board vote to the City's deed is 40.5 days; none was recorded before the vote. 4 properties changed hands two or more times in the four years before the vote. At 490 South Van Ness Avenue the owner since 2009 deeded the property to four different holders between 22 December 2014 and 20 March 2015, months before the Board approved paying $18,037,500; the City's deed came from one of them. 1000 Sutter Street changed hands 3 times in the four years before a City grantee bought it with City-linked financing.","how":"Each parcel of each purchase in the site’s “Property deals” page was searched by block and lot in the Assessor-Recorder's index and the print read line by line. A deed is a document titled DEED or TRUSTEE'S DEED. The City's deed is the one whose grantee is the City and whose grantor is not; the seller's own acquisition is the latest earlier deed whose grantee is the City deed's grantor. Transfers are deeds in the four years up to the Board vote. The Board vote is the day of the Board of Supervisors' final action on the file (adopted or finally passed) in the vote history; where the history has no such action, the day the file was introduced is shown and the row says so. The median counts only purchases with a vote date. (Before 21 November 2026 this screen counted from the day each file was introduced.)","limits":"The index gives no price, so what each seller paid is still unknown. Deeds between related entities, estate transfers and splits into shares for a tax-deferred exchange all count as transfers and are common in ordinary commercial sales. A deed long after the vote usually reflects due diligence, financing or a later closing the Board allowed. Where the City's deed is missing, the parcel was probably renumbered after a condominium or parcel map. Titles of several documents recorded on the same day can be attributed to the neighbouring entry when the print stacks them; deeds were checked against the owner's own list (the “ALL DEEDS” table) and agree.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"building","t":"Building","type":"text"},{"k":"approved","t":"Board vote","type":"date"},{"k":"price","t":"Price","type":"usd"},{"k":"cityDeed","t":"Deed to the buyer recorded","type":"date"},{"k":"lagDays","t":"Days after vote","type":"days"},{"k":"grantor","t":"Signed over by","type":"text"},{"k":"sellerTook","t":"That owner took title","type":"date"},{"k":"daysHeld","t":"Days held at vote","type":"days"},{"k":"transfers4y","t":"Transfers in 4 years","type":"int"},{"k":"chain","t":"Those transfers","type":"text"},{"k":"cityDoc","t":"Document","type":"text"},{"k":"note","t":"Note","type":"text"},{"k":"file","t":"Board file","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"building":"490 South Van Ness Avenue","approved":"2015-07-28","price":18037500,"cityDeed":"2015-08-28","cityDoc":"2015125770","voted":true,"lagDays":31,"grantor":"BENICIA LAKE LLC","sellerTook":"2014-12-22","daysHeld":218,"transfers4y":4,"chain":"2014-12-22 J C N DEVELOPERS LLC to SOUTH VAN NESS 490 LP; 2014-12-22 J C N DEVELOPERS LLC to BENECIA LAKE LLC; 2014-12-22 J C N DEVELOPERS LLC to MUNSTER PROPERTY HOLDING INC; 2015-03-20 J C N DEVELOPERS LLC to a person","note":"","file":{"t":"File 150734","u":"https://sfgov.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=2369794&GUID=0216C1E7-8ACA-48BB-8D95-57AAD91347EF"}},{"building":"1000 Sutter Street (Hotel Granada) (bought by Episcopal Community Services)","approved":"2020-10-06","price":null,"cityDeed":"2020-11-13","cityDoc":"2020048495","voted":true,"lagDays":38,"grantor":"655-685 4TH STREET LP","sellerTook":"2019-07-25","daysHeld":439,"transfers4y":3,"chai